  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1208 AM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nOur seemingly endless stretch of abnormal heat still has no end \nin sight, as model trends continue to show upper level ridging \ndominating the synoptic pattern. Both deterministic and ensemble \ndatasets depict high pressure being nudged eastward over the \nsoutheast CONUS through the week, and then morphing back on top of\nthe Plains this weekend as persistent troughing settles atop the \nPacific northwest. Moisture transport to the Panhandles will be \nscarce this week, while high temperatures steadily remain in the \n90 to 105 range each day. If there are any better rain chances, \nmodels suggest mid week could see slightly improved potential as \nthe jet stream sags closer to the Panhandles. However, this still \nonly supports meager 10-20% POPs to far northwestern portions of \nthe forecast area. \n\nHarrel",
